            "no_desc_withouthtml": "<p>Filmmaker Shakeel Noorani was arrested by Mumbai Police on Saturday in connection with a rape, sexual assault and blackmail case filed by a 33-year-old actor. The 73-year-old filmmaker was arrested from a farmhouse in Maharashtra's Satara district after allegedly evading arrest for around 40 days.</p><p>Noorani was arrested by the Malwani police and is currently in police custody. A case has been registered against him under relevant sections of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita. His lawyer, however, has denied the allegations against him.</p><p>According to the police complaint, the actor first came in contact with Noorani in 2016 and alleged that he sexually exploited her repeatedly over the years. She further alleged that Noorani drugged her and recorded videos of her in compromising situations.</p><p>She also alleged that Noorani blackmailed her by threatening to make the videos public. According to her complaint, she suffered a miscarriage as a result of the alleged incidents.</p><p>Following the complaint, the police registered a case and launched an investigation to trace Noorani. He was subsequently arrested from a farmhouse in Satara district after allegedly remaining untraceable for around 40 days.</p><p>Deputy Commissioner of Police Sandeep Ghuge confirmed Noorani's arrest. \"We have arrested him and we are investigating this case as per law,\" he said.</p><p>Noorani has been associated with Bollywood films including <em>Bade Dilwala</em> (1999) and <em>Joru Ka Ghulam</em> (2000).</p><p>The investigation is currently underway, and the allegations against Noorani are yet to be established in court.</p>",
            "no_author": {
              "a_title": "Dipesh D. Tripathi"
            }
          },
